    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T22:40:04Z",
    "body": "**Hands-on check on macOS, release build of this branch.** The test job is a Circular op whose 0.8 mm helix produces \"feed moves cross\" warnings, with a Face and a 2D Contour beside it.\n\n1. The warned Circular moves draw in the gouge colour, with a cross marker on the warning group's first move.\n2. The two ops with no warnings (Face, 2D Contour) draw exactly as before, with their normal feed/rapid/plunge colours.\n3. On the op page, the folded warning line (\"feed moves 2 and 2075 cross … repeated on 9 more moves\") is underlined. Hover shows \"show this move in the viewport\".\n4. Clicking that line centres the camera on the move, with zoom and orientation kept.\n\nNot exercised by hand: a plain entry-note line not being clickable. This job has none; the behaviour is pinned by `banner_tests::a_located_warning_line_reports_its_click_and_a_plain_line_does_not`.\n\n**Merge and gate:** upstream/main merged (clean), then `scripts/gate.sh quick`.\n- All pins pass: the `warned_moves`, `path_lines`, `warning_fold` and `banner_tests` tests.\n- Every red reproduces on upstream main:\n  - `probe_op` (#344, fixed by #345);\n  - the GPU headless tests;\n  - the `egui_shell_snapshot_light` and `tool_editor_snapshot` goldens. These are anti-aliasing-level diffs, #255.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
